###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - This is the paper that introduces SchNet (NeurIPS 2017) and ISO17; the registry origin of SchNet is moved from schutt2018 (the JCP follow-up, a legacy file) to this paper. No derivation from an earlier registry method is stated. The origin-paper stub of this paper is removed from origin-papers.csv now that the paper is encoded.
# - The level of theory of ISO17 is not stated in this paper. The text says 129 isomers and 645,000 examples; unke2019 describes 127 isomers.
# - The architecture (interaction blocks, feature sizes, cutoff) is in the supplement, which is not part of the version read; only the optimiser settings of Sec. 5 are encoded.
# - The mean-predictor baseline of Table 3 is not encoded.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: datacite).
